## 3. Key Notes for Staff and Volunteers

- **Registration Desk:** Ensure all new students receive their welcome kits and ID badges upon check-in. Late arrivals should be directed to the help desk.
- **Room Assignments:** Double-check updated room allocations for breakout sessions. Signs will be placed outside each room to avoid confusion.
- **Technical Support:** The IT team will be on standby during the dean's keynote speech and the Q&A session to address any audiovisual issues.
- **Campus Tours:** Group leaders must arrive 15 minutes before their scheduled time. Maps and itineraries will be provided at the main lobby.
- **Social Mixer:** Ensure refreshments are replenished regularly. Volunteers should encourage students to participate in networking activities.

---

## 4. Additional Updates

- **Audiovisual Equipment:** Additional microphones and projectors have been allocated for the dean's opening lecture.
- **Pamphlet Reprint:** The corrected pamphlets will be distributed to all staff by 7:30 AM on orientation day. Please discard any outdated versions.
- **Welcome Email:** The communications team has confirmed that the welcome email, including a personal note from the dean, will be sent to all new students at 12:00 PM.
- **RA and TA Applications:** Administration staff are reminded to follow up on flagged applications with discrepancies in recommendation letters.

